.TH AGENTMOVE 1 "2026-08-05" "agentmove-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agentmove \- move your AI agent between clients: config, MCP servers, skills, memory, persona
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agentmove
[\fB--home\fR \fIdir\fR]
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agentmove
migrates AI agent setups between OpenClaw, Hermes Agent, Claude Code, Claude
Desktop, Codex
CLI, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, Cline, Zed, OpenHands, GitHub Copilot CLI, OpenCode, Qwen Code, Amp, VS Code, Kiro, Roo Code, Continue, Crush, goose, Antigravity, Droid, Amazon Q Developer CLI, Warp, Junie, LM Studio, Trae, CodeBuddy, Qoder CLI, Auggie CLI, Kilo Code, Kimi Code CLI, Grok CLI, Vibe Code CLI, Nanocoder, and Jan \(em in any direction, through a portable bundle
format. Imports are dry-run by default, existing files are backed up before
writing, likely secrets are redacted on export, and every lossy mapping is
reported as a warning.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B export \fIclient\fR [\fB-o\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB--include-secrets\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Export a client's setup into a portable bundle directory (default
\fI./agentmove-bundle\fR).
.TP
.B import \fIclient\fR [\fB-i\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB--apply\fR] [\fB--replace-mcp\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Import a bundle into a client. Dry-run by default; \fB--apply\fR writes files
after backing up existing ones to \fI~/.agentmove/backups/<timestamp>/\fR.
Imported MCP servers are merged into the target's existing list;
\fB--replace-mcp\fR replaces it entirely.
.TP
.B convert \fIfrom\fR \fIto\fR [\fB--apply\fR] [\fB--include-secrets\fR] [\fB--replace-mcp\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Export + import in one step, without leaving a bundle on disk.
.TP
.B diff \fIfrom\fR \fIto\fR [\fB--json\fR]
Layer-by-layer structural comparison between two clients, or between a bundle
directory and a client.
.TP
.B pack \fIbundle\fR [\fB-o\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Encrypt a bundle directory into a single portable \fI.agentpack\fR file
(AES-256-GCM, key derived from the \fBAGENTMOVE_PASSPHRASE\fR environment
variable via scrypt) for carrying an agent across machines.
.TP
.B unpack \fIfile\fR [\fB-o\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
Decrypt an agentpack file back into a bundle directory. \fBimport -i\fR also
accepts an agentpack file directly.
.TP
.B doctor [\fB--json\fR]
Detect installed clients and inventory what agentmove can migrate from each.
.TP
.B clients [\fB--json\fR]
List supported clients and their default config locations.
.TP
.B completion \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIfish\fR
Print a shell completion script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --home \fIdir\fR
Override the home directory (useful for testing and staging).
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable JSON output (plans, warnings, per-layer summary).
.TP
.B --only \fIlayers\fR
Comma-separated subset of layers to migrate:
\fImcp\fR, \fIskills\fR, \fImemory\fR, \fIinstructions\fR, \fIpersona\fR
(on \fBexport\fR, \fBimport\fR, and \fBconvert\fR).
.TP
.B --project \fIdir\fR
Operate on the client's project-scoped files inside \fIdir\fR instead of the
home directory: \fB.mcp.json\fR/\fBCLAUDE.md\fR (claude-code),
\fBAGENTS.md\fR (codex), \fB.gemini/settings.json\fR/\fBGEMINI.md\fR (gemini),
\fB.cursor/mcp.json\fR/\fB.cursor/rules\fR (cursor), \fB.windsurf/rules\fR
(windsurf), \fB.clinerules\fR (cline), \fB.zed/settings.json\fR/\fB.rules\fR
(zed), \fB.openhands/microagents\fR+\fB.openhands/skills\fR (openhands),
\fB.mcp.json\fR+\fB.github/copilot-instructions.md\fR (copilot),
\fBopencode.json\fR+\fBAGENTS.md\fR+\fB.opencode/skills\fR (opencode),
\fB.qwen/settings.json\fR+\fBQWEN.md\fR+\fB.qwen/skills\fR (qwen),
\fB.goosehints\fR+\fB.goose/memory\fR+\fB.agents/skills\fR (goose),
\fB.amp/settings.json\fR+\fBAGENTS.md\fR+\fB.agents/skills\fR (amp),
\fB.vscode/mcp.json\fR+\fB.github/copilot-instructions.md\fR (vscode),
\fB.kiro/settings/mcp.json\fR+\fB.kiro/steering/\fR+\fB.kiro/skills/\fR (kiro);
\fB.roo/mcp.json\fR+\fB.roo/rules/\fR+\fB.roo/skills/\fR (roo);
\fB.continue/mcpServers/\fR+\fB.continue/rules/\fR (continue);
\fBcrush.json\fR/\fB.crush.json\fR+\fBCRUSH.md\fR+\fB.crush/skills/\fR (crush);
\fB.agents/mcp_config.json\fR+\fB.agents/rules/\fR+\fB.agents/skills/\fR (antigravity).
Backups go to
\fIdir\fR/.agentmove/backups. openclaw/hermes have no project scope.
.TP
.B --mif \fIfile\fR
On \fBexport\fR, additionally write the memory layer as a vendor-neutral MIF v2
document. On \fBimport\fR, import the memory layer from a MIF document instead
of a bundle.
.TP
.B --debug
Print a full stack trace on unexpected errors (also enabled by the
\fBAGENTMOVE_DEBUG=1\fR environment variable).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (e.g. unknown client).
.TP
.B 3
Bad input data (missing or corrupt bundle or config; the message includes the
offending file path).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.agentmove/backups/
Automatic backups taken before \fB--apply\fR writes.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation at
.UR https://agentmove.zalize.com
.UE .
